14|// ⛔ CONFIDENCE IS NOT AN EVIDENCE TIER, AND TWO VERBS RANKED BY IT.
15|//
16|// Measured on the pinned click arm:
17|//
18|//     EXTRACTED     n=10976   conf 0.75..1.00  (avg 0.933)
19|//     LSP_VERIFIED  n=1460    conf 0.95..0.95  (avg 0.950)
20|//     AMBIGUOUS     n=1145    conf 0.75..0.95  (avg 0.930)
21|//
22|// The ranges overlap and the averages are indistinguishable, so `ORDER BY confidence DESC LIMIT n`
23|// cannot rank tiers — the candidates tie and SQLite breaks the tie arbitrarily.
24|//
25|// ⛔ WHAT THAT DID TO THE DELETION-SAFETY VERB. `graph_preflight("Context")` rendered five
26|// EXTRACTED callers, every one of them from a test file, while 124 LSP_VERIFIED callers existed on
27|// that same symbol in that same graph. The verified evidence was not missing — it lost a coin toss
28|// and was never shown. After the fix the same call returns five LSP_VERIFIED callers in
29|// src/click/core.py, each tagged.
30|//
31|// ⛔⛔ AND THE READER COULD NOT HAVE TOLD. `preflight` and `graph_file` build their edge lines by
32|// hand — `conf=` and nothing else — while the other eight verbs route through the shared renderer
33|// that tags provenance. `preflight`'s query SELECTED `e.provenance` and the render dropped it, so a
34|// heuristic caller and a compiler-verified one printed as byte-identical strings. That is the
35|// original "EXTRACTED and AMBIGUOUS are indistinguishable" finding, which was withdrawn TWICE after
36|// checking the shared renderer — the one place where it was already false.
37|//
38|// ⇒ The fixture below is built so confidence ALONE picks the wrong rows: the heuristic edges carry
39|// HIGHER confidence than the verified ones. A verb that still sorts by confidence returns the
40|// heuristic set and fails.
41|
42|describe('evidence tier outranks confidence, and the tier is visible', () => {
43|  let repoRoot;
44|
45|  beforeEach(async () => {
46|    repoRoot = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'apg-tier-'));
47|    const run = (...args) => execFileSync('git', ['-C', repoRoot, ...args], { stdio: 'ignore' });
48|    run('init', '-q');
49|    run('-c', 'user.email=t@t', '-c', 'user.name=t', 'commit', '--allow-empty', '-m', 'init');
50|    mkdirSync(join(repoRoot, '.aify-graph'), { recursive: true });
51|    const commit = execFileSync('git', ['-C', repoRoot, 'rev-parse', 'HEAD'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim();
52|    writeFileSync(join(repoRoot, '.aify-graph', 'manifest.json'), JSON.stringify({
53|      commit, indexedAt: new Date().toISOString(), nodes: 0, edges: 0,
54|      schemaVersion: 4, extractorVersion: '0.1.0',
55|      status: 'ok', dirtyFiles: [], dirtyEdges: [], dirtyEdgeCount: 0,
56|    }));
57|
58|    const db = openDb(join(repoRoot, '.aify-graph', 'graph.sqlite'));
59|    try {
60|      const node = (id, label, file_path) => ({
61|        id, type: 'Function', label, file_path,
62|        start_line: 1, end_line: 1, language: 'python', confidence: 1,
63|        structural_fp: '', dependency_fp: '', extra: {},
64|      });
65|      upsertNode(db, node('fn:target', 'target', 'src/target.py'));
66|      // graph_file resolves a File node, then queries the symbols declared in it.
67|      upsertNode(db, { ...node('file:target', 'target.py', 'src/target.py'), type: 'File' });
68|
69|      // ⛔ THE INVERSION, MADE EXPLICIT. Six heuristic callers at conf=1.00, two verified at 0.95.
70|      // Sorted by confidence the verified pair is last and falls outside every top-5. Sorted by
71|      // tier it leads. Real graphs tie at 0.95 instead, which is the same defect with a coin toss
72|      // in place of a guarantee — this fixture just makes the failure deterministic.
73|      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i += 1) {
